/target
/runs
/.trace
*.profraw
reports/trace-phase-manual.html

# Benchmark results ARE committed -- the git history of your scores is part of
# the artifact. But not the per-attempt scratch workspaces: each one carries
# its own `git init`, which is ~400 files of nothing. The trajectory records
# what happened, and the workspace is reproducible from the task seed.
bench/runs/**/workspace/

# Secrets. Never commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A returned result belongs in bench/runs, not loose in the tree.
/trace-results.md
/trial.md
